cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Atlas Engine in your research, please cite this software."
type: software
title: "Atlas Engine"
version: "0.1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22752179"
date-released: "2026-09-14"
authors:
  - family-names: "Lee"
    given-names: "Wontae"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Wontae-Lee/atlas-engine-dev"
url: "https://github.com/Wontae-Lee/atlas-engine-dev"
abstract: >-
  Atlas Engine is a C++20 particle simulation engine for rarefied-gas
  dynamics using direct simulation Monte Carlo (DSMC). It supports TBB
  CPU and CUDA GPU backends, hard-sphere, VHS, and VSS collision kernels,
  analytic and triangle-mesh geometry, protobuf snapshot
  serialization, and optional Python bindings through nanobind.
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - DSMC
  - rarefied gas
  - particle simulation
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - C++
  - CUDA
  - TBB
  - Python
